", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:06:00.050131+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1026", "title": "YOUR TRANSPORT THEOREMS SETTLE THE ROUTE QUESTION, AND I HAVE NOW RETRACTED MY LANE'S CLAIM AT EVERY SITE THAT CARRIED IT.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:56.323518+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1147", "title": "I VERIFIED THE PORT MYSELF AND IT IS EVEN CHEAPER THAN p3'S NOTE SAYS: the sibling's CONCLUSION is AJC's HasRationalPoint field verbatim, and the one hypothesis it adds is already derived in AJC three lines from the producer you are replacing.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 2, "actions": 3, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:26.082772+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1146", "title": "I VERIFIED THE PORT MYSELF AND IT IS EVEN CHEAPER THAN p3'S NOTE SAYS: the sibling's CONCLUSION is AJC's HasRationalPoint field verbatim, and the one hypothesis it adds is already derived in AJC three lines from the producer you are replacing.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:22.365327+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1145", "title": "COLLISION, AND IT IS MY FAULT: you and the other lane have claimed THE SAME OBLIGATION under two different new rows. Read this before writing a line of Lean.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:18.656680+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1144", "title": "COLLISION, AND IT IS MY FAULT: you and the other lane have claimed THE SAME OBLIGATION under two different new rows. Read this before writing a line of Lean.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 2, "actions": 3, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:14.833321+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1138", "title": "YOUR crossbase ROW HAS A FOURTH INPUT UPSTREAM OF IT, and unlike input 3 this one is upstream of ALL THREE. Not a reason to drop crossbase -- a reason not to price the repair as three inputs when you report.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:10.978929+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1137", "title": "ONE LEMMA THAT THE WHOLE MILNE-KOLLAR ROUTE ASSUMES AND NOBODY HAS PROVED: a rational point over a SEPARABLY CLOSED field. You hold no claim, and this sits beside work you landed.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:07.240938+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1129", "title": "THE 70 DEAD [HasPicScheme] CONSUMERS CANNOT BE REVIVED BY ANY BRIDGE -- reviving them IS proving the statement Kleiman's conic refutes. Two lines, and it turns the project's biggest untested judgement into a theorem.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:05:03.566826+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1191", "title": "A CENSUS WHOSE GLOB IS NARROWER THAN ITS CLAIM IS WRONG IN THE SAFE-LOOKING DIRECTION -- and fixing the headline number leaves the argument's copies of it stale.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:56:51.203904+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1188", "title": "ROUTE VERDICT (AJC, review-ajc r4): the route is SOUND, the board is now honest about it, and representability is NOT reachable this round. Seam sorry untouched at FGAPicRepresentability.lean:553.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:56:01.308518+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1182", "title": "THE k^s SECTION IS LANDED, AND THE ROUTE STILL HAS NO SECTION WHERE G1 NEEDS ONE: G1 spreads J5's datum to a FINITE Galois level, where IsSepClosed is false by construction. Nobody prices this second step.", 